.Dd $Mdocdate$
.Dt BUILD.SH 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm build.sh
.Nd build, flash, lint, clean, check status, or open a debug console for the Spacecentricity keymap (QMK firmware)
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar keymap_name
.Op Fl c | Fl -clean | Fl -clear
.Op Fl -clean-only | Fl -clear-only
.Op Fl C | Fl -check
.Op Fl d | Fl -console
.Op Fl f | Fl -flash
.Op Fl l | Fl -lint
.Op Fl n | Fl -no-banner | Fl -skip-banner
.Op Fl S | Fl -strict
.Op Fl s | Fl -status
.Op Fl v | Fl -verbose | Fl -verbose Ns = Ns Ar N
.Op Fl h | Fl -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is an optional POSIX-compliant convenience wrapper for building, cleaning,
flashing, linting, checking the symlink/QMK status, and opening a debug
.Pp
This script streamlines common workflows into a single-command
interface by reducing repetitive steps and cognitive overhead.
.Pp
By default:
.Bl -bullet
.It
The keymap name is
.Sq spacecentricity .
.It
The QMK checkout is assumed to be at
.Pa $HOME/qmk_firmware .
.El
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl c , Fl -clean , Fl -clear
Remove QMK build artifacts before building.
.It Fl -clean-only , Fl -clear-only
Clean build artifacts and exit without building.
.It Fl C , Fl -check
Run a symlink/status check and a strict lint pass together, then exit.
Equivalent to running
.Fl -status
followed by
.Fl -lint Fl -strict .
.It Fl d , Fl -console
Open the QMK HID debug console
.Pq Ic qmk console
to view live debug output from the keyboard, then exit.
.It Fl f , Fl -flash
Build and flash the firmware.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Show the help message and exit.
.It Fl l , Fl -lint
Lint the keymap before building.
.It Fl n , Fl -no-banner , Fl -skip-banner
Suppress the ASCII art banner for this invocation.
Overrides
.Ev SPACECENTRICITY_BANNER
when set.
.It Fl S , Fl -strict
Treat lint warnings as errors.
This option affects the lint operation and requires
.Fl -lint .
.It Fl s , Fl -status
Show symlink/QMK status and exit.
.It Fl v , Fl -verbose
Show full, live
.Ic qmk compile
output during the build instead of the default spinner and elapsed-time
indicator.
.It Fl -verbose Ns = Ns Ar N
.Ar N
lines of live
.Ic qmk compile
output during the build, redrawn in place as the build progresses.
.Pp
If
.Ar N
exceeds the current terminal height, or the terminal height cannot be
determined, this falls back to the same full-output behavior as
.Fl -verbose
with no argument.
If
.Ar N
is not a valid non-negative integer, a warning is printed and the same
fallback occurs.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev QMK_PATH
Path to your QMK firmware checkout.
Defaults to
.Pa $HOME/qmk_firmware .
.It Ev SPACECENTRICITY_BANNER
Set to
.Sq false
or
.Sq 0
to suppress the ASCII art banner by default, without needing
.Fl -no-banner
on every invocation.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal
build.sh                  # Build spacecentricity
build.sh -f               # Build and flash spacecentricity
build.sh --no-banner -f   # Build and flash without the banner
build.sh my_keymap_name   # Build a given keymap name
build.sh --clean --flash  # Clean build artifacts, then flash spacecentricity
build.sh --check          # Verify symlink and lint cleanliness together
build.sh -d               # Open the QMK debug console
build.sh --console        # Same as above
build.sh -v               # Build with full live qmk compile output
build.sh --verbose=10     # Build with a scrolling 10-line output window
QMK_PATH=~/Projects/qmk_firmware build.sh -s  # Display status w/ custom QMK path
SPACECENTRICITY_BANNER=false build.sh         # Skip banner via environment variable
.Ed
.Sh TIPS
Use the stub in the project's root to invoke
.Pa scripts/build.sh
directly. For example, to build and flash the keyboard firmware:
.Pp
.Dl ./build -f
.Pp
Think of this script as a convenient command grammar for common
QMK operations.
.Pp
For a quick peek at compile progress without the full firehose of
.Ic qmk compile
output, try
.Fl -verbose Ns = Ns Ar N
with a small
.Ar N .
